  offerDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - Now you understand how a beam bridge works.
    - You've also learned about the load your bridge needs to carry and the materials
      available for construction.
    - It's time to apply what you've learned.
    - Your first project will be a simple crossing between two sides of the canyon.
    - I think you're ready for your first <b><#E09500>contract</color></b>.
    - Oh, and there's one more thing you should know before accepting your first contract.
    - Throughout your journey, you'll encounter different <b><#E09500>engineering lessons</color></b>.
    - After completing the bridge construction and testing, you'll take a short <b><#E09500>quiz</color></b>
      to review what you've learned.
    - These quizzes will be part of your <b><#E09500>training projects</color></b> and
      <b><#E09500>main contracts</color></b> that introduce engineering lessons.
    - <b><#E09500>Side Quests</color></b>, however, are optional challenges where you
      can practice your skills without taking a quiz.
    - So pay attention to each lesson. You'll need that knowledge not only to build
      your bridges, but also to answer the questions afterward.
    - Now, are you ready to take your first contract?
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - Your first contract is a simple bridge construction project.
    - The crossing ahead needs a safe and reliable connection between both sides
      of the canyon.
    - You'll use the <b><#E09500>Beam Bridge</color></b> design we just discussed.
    - Your job is to construct the bridge and make sure it can safely carry the
      <b><#E09500>200 kg vehicle</color></b>.
    - Remember, the roadway must be properly supported, and your design must stay
      within the available budget.
    - Review the contract carefully before entering Build Mode.
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - You can now go to the <b><#E09500>construction site</color></b> whenever you
      are ready.
    - Enter the <b><#E09500>Blueprint</color></b> and begin construction.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - Good work, {PlayerName}.
    - Your first training bridge has passed its test.
    - You now know how to accept a <b><#E09500>contract</color></b>, use the <b><#E09500>blueprint</color></b>,
      build a bridge, and test your design.
    - But your work is not finished yet.
    - An engineer should inspect the structure after construction.
    - Open your <b><#E09500>Almanac</color></b> and review your first entry.
